Mr. Fun wrote:
> 
> Sounds like you know something about these old DECs.  I have 100's of
> Floppy disks with data on them that were written to on a DEC PDP11/83
> running RT-11 OS.  I think the disks are formated to about 1.2 Meg.
> Do you know of any program that will allow these disks to be read in
> an IBM PC floppy disk drive?  I'm going to be selling the DEC system
> in a couple of months (it's part of a larger system) and after that I
> won't have any way to read the data disks unless I can find a way to
> read them in a PC or else buy some old DEC to use to read them.
> I don't recall the exact floppy disk format that was used, seems like
> there was two possible kinds, RX-50 and something else.  We use
> regular IBM PC HD (1.2 meg) floppies and my memory says they format
> out to 2400 blocks.  If that's critical I can find out next week.
> 
> If you can provide any insight or info I'd appreciate it.
> 
> Jim
> 

Hi Jim,

   It sounds like you have an RX33 drive, which is a "standard" 1.2 MB
double sided "PC compatable" drive.  This drive uses the same sector
formats as a PC HD drive and should be physically readable on most PCs.

   The problem is not with reading the bits, the problem is with
converting the bits.  The disks you have are NOT using the MS/DOS file
system, it is using what ever file system is native to the O/S you are
running (you didn't specify).  Possible file systems are RT-11 format,
RSTS - DOS format, or RSX-11 ODS-1 format.  These different file
systems  define things like directory structure, how blocks are alocated
to files, file name formats, etc...  

   There are tools available on PCs that know how to read disks from
different operating systems, so it's not as bad as it sounds.  Of course
if you have binary data files, you will probably have to write a custom
conversion program to convert the data from whatever program wrote it to
a format that your PC's program can use.  Text files are not too much
trouble, but sometimes you have problems with carriage controls.

   Anyway, good luck.

-- 
