David C. Jenner <djenner@halcyon.com> wrote:
>I picked up a DEC VT330 terminal without a keyboard.  I believe the
>standard keyboard for this model is an LK-401.  I have lots of LK-201s,
>and that model seems to work OK.  But what I am "missing" by not having
>the LK-401?

The standard keyboard on the VT330 was the LK201.  The 401 didn't show
up on a video terminal (or anything much for that matter) until the VT420.

The LK401 has separate "alt" keys, but is otherwise pretty much the same
functionally as the LK201.  This is useful on workstations, where the LK201
required that the Compose key actually act as Alt, and the compose character
function assigned to Alt-Space.  I don't think the alt keys do anything if 
you hook an LK401 to a VT3xx terminal.

