In article <67m2bs$srn@usenet.pa.dec.com>, hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.nospam (Hoff Hoffman) writes
>   And yes, any VT-series terminal will work as a console terminal on
>   these systems.

If you're using a VT-52, make certain you have jumper W5 installed; without
this jumper, all characters sent from the VT-52 appear to have bit 7 set.

Also, most VAXen these days (I'm pretty certain the 2000 also does this)
issue escape sequences to the terminal to ask the terminal to identify
itself. These sequences put a VT-52 into hold screen mode (ESC [ is the
magic enter hold screen mode sequence for the VT-52), so you usually have
to power cycle the VT-52 after the machine has given you the >>> prompt.
The H19 is a bit nicer than a VT-52 here because it has a reset button.

(He did say "any VT-series terminal"...)
