Peter Mardahl wrote:

> I'm running Digital UNIX 4.0C on the machine, and I'd like
> to try the 1600x1200 screen resolution.  The board and
> the monitor are capable of it.
>
> Anyone know the incantation?  'man -k' is getting me
> nowhere.
>

The short answer is that it should be documented in the Open3D release
note. Check them in /usr/lib/OPEN3D.

You need to add some arguments to the X Server command line. The easiest
place to do this is in /usr/lib/X11/Xserver.conf. Tthere are other
places to put them that are windowing environment specific that
accomplish the same thing. Putting them here will handle both CDE and
the ol DECWindows environment.

Edit the file using your favorite editor.  Look for lines in the file
that look like -
args <
! Cateye Server args start
    -pn -nice -2 -bs -su
! Cateye Server args end
    -pn
>

If you have a PowerStorm 4D40T/50T/60T, the release notes say to use the
"-screen" and "-vsync" options
to set the screen resolution and the vertical refresh rate. Append them
to the arguments. (after -bs -su).

You will then have to restart the X Server. Log out. At the CDE
"dtlogin" screen, hit and hold the "Options" button and choose "Rset
Login Screen". This should restart the X Server at the new resolution.

Hope this helps
