The history of these is,

DE500-XA
DE500-AA
DE500-BA

Each has had a progressively improved chip incorporated in it's design to
take into account the still emerging standards of 100mb/sec ethernet.

21040
21040a
21140
21140a
21142

if my memory serves me. And within a particular card, improved chips as well.

In any event, it still appears that the standards for autonegotiation and
half/full duplex rate negotiation are still different from one vendors
network hardware to another, and thus the reasons why you still have to do
some fiddling to get Full Duplex.

On another note, support for the latest cards is being and has been added
to a number of systems, the latest Firmware CD-ROM is V5.0, thus V3.9 is a
little old, 2 versions old.

The latest firmware for all Alpha Systems is available from
www.digital.com. Also, interim releases are to be found there as well.

