Jill Johnson wrote:
> 
> Hi All,
>         I have a Dec Alpha 1000 with a Etherworks Turbo PCI ethernet
> card.  I just installed Digital Unix 4.0c on this thing and now it
> think it wants to use the AUI port instead of the 10BaseT....does
> anyone know how to fix this?  I know it's not jumpers because before
> I installed the new OS it worked just fine on the 10BaseT.  Thanks
> in advance for any help you can lend.  It's probably something super
> simple, but this is my first time installing Digital Unix.

At the console prompt (>>>) type SHOW EWA0_MODE.  Make sure it's set to
what you want.  If you type SET EWA0_MODE you'll get a list of options.
Make sure to INIT after you change it and before booting the O/S.  Also,
make sure the appropriate cables are connected before you INIT.

--

