Thanx to Tim Shoppa & Terry Kennedy for their quick response to my questions 
about making an XXDP-XM bootable diagnostics tape from a disk. I am running a 
PDP-11/44, with an RP06 drive and a TU-77 tape drive. The procedure I am 
using:

	>>> B DB0:

	      .  R UPDAT

* ZERO MM0:

	      * CREATE MM0:

	      * PIP MM0:=DB0:

	      * EXIT
      .

The resulting tape is made at 800 bpi and boots the extended monitor fine, so 
I know that the PIP command that copies it from disk must be good, unlike the 
EXACT same procedure as above, but with the word FILE in place of PIP. The 
FILE copy resulted in an unbootable tape. Both of the COPY commands, under 
UPDAT and at the extended monitor prompt("."), give "invalid device" messages, 
so I am trying the ASG command under UPDAT in case the routine just doesn't 
like two devices with the same number. Also, there is the ENABLE command under 
UPDAT, which enables another device for system use. The command * E MM0: <CR> 
gives back only the * prompt as a response but doesn't seem to affect the 
"invalid device" messages on the COPY commands. Thanx again for the help.

Happy Holidays.

Harry Mason
AV8B Flight Simulators
MCAS Cherry Point




