formatter ZRJBD0.BIC on a PDP-11/44. I did it this way:

>>> B DB	(booting the XXDP-XM diagnostic pack)
     . R UPDAT
     * ZERO MM0:
     * CREATE MM0:	(builds the XXDPSM small monitor on tape)
     * EXIT
     . <CTRL  - P>
>>> H
>>> I
>>> B DB	(booting the XXDP+ diagnostic pack)
     . R UPD2
     * FILE MM0:=DB0:	(copying first few files from XXDP+ diagnostics 
			 pack, including UPD2)
     * EXIT
     . <CTRL - P>
>>> B MM	(booting the tape just made - boots the XXDP-SM mall 
		 monitor)
     . R UPD2	(just copied from the XXDP+ disk to tape)
     * FILE MM0:=DB0:ZRJBD0.BIC	(copying the RP06 disk formatter program to 
				 tape)
     * EXIT
     . R ZRJB??	(this starts the formatter program successfully)

So, I have a tape that is bootable, thanks to XXDP-XM, but otherwise 
contains only XXDP+ files. How can I get the XXDP+ bootstrap monitor onto a 
tape? Are the XXDP+ SAVE and SAVEM commands (replaced by the XXDP-XM CREATE 
command) the answer? Does anyone know the syntax for these commands? I am 
having trouble with device names. Is the problem perhaps  that XXDP+ does 
not support device name MM0:?

