In article <40441BF0AC0B8748.AC2609477321F77D.F5E4DACDE528197B@library-proxy.airnews.net>, "Robert Young" <rcyoung@groupz.net> writes:
:I need the syntax for the boot command used in bringing up standalone backup
:from a TK50 tape for a Vax 4000-200. Anyone have it handy??

  Here are a few console commands that can be used on most (all?) VAX
  systems from the last decade or so:

	>>> SHOW DEVICE
	>>> SHOW CONFIG
	>>> BOOT

  The following two are the primary tape and disk bootstraps for many
  systems -- the particular device prefix and unit number can change,
  however:

	>>> BOOT MUA0
	>>> BOOT DUA0

  And here is my own personal favorite :-) -- the one console command
  I tend to use the most in these situations:

	>>> HELP

  And you might want to check out the installation and upgrade manuals,
  available at http://www.openvms.digital.com:81/ -- the upgrade manuals
  usually contain the system-specific information needed for a standalone
  BACKUP, as it is the sort of task performed during an upgrade...

