What CSR did you install the UC07 at?  What other devices are in the
system?  The console microcode on the KA630 generall expects devices
to be installed according to the "standard" CSR/vector rules that
DEC adopted in the late 70's for Unibus and Q-bus devices.  These
rules are explained (though maybe not too clearly) in the Emulex UC07
manual.  The KA630 device-finding routine is actually a bit more
lenient than the strict DEC CSR configuration rules, and sometimes
will let you get away with things that aren't officially correct.
Other times, the OS will find things that aren't officially correct
and aren't found by the KA630 boot command.  The best solution, of
course, is to install all devices at their canonical CSR's, and then
everything will find them.

The rules can be complicated.  In particular, if you have a system with
two MSCP disk controllers and two DHV11's, they live at the following
CSR's:

SYSGEN>  CONFIG
DEVICE> dhv11 2
DEVICE> uda50 2
DEVICE>  Exit
Device: UDA     Name: PUA        CSR: 772150     Vector: 154    Support: yes
Device: UDA     Name: PUB        CSR: 760334*    Vector: 300*   Support: yes
Device: DHV11   Name: TXA        CSR: 760500*    Vector: 310*   Support: yes
Device: DHV11   Name: TXB        CSR: 760520*    Vector: 320*   Support: yes

But if you've got DZ11's instead of DHV11's, things are different enough
to confuse things:

DEVICE> dz11 2
DEVICE> uda50 2
%SYSGEN-I-EQV_NOTICE, equivalent name - device UDA50 will be output as UDA
DEVICE>  Exit
Device: UDA     Name: PUA        CSR: 772150     Vector: 154    Support: yes
Device: DZ11    Name: TTA        CSR: 760100*    Vector: 300*   Support: yes
Device: DZ11    Name: TTB        CSR: 760110*    Vector: 310*   Support: yes
Device: UDA     Name: PUB        CSR: 760354*    Vector: 320*   Support: yes

You haven't given us nearly enough information about your system and
its options to tell you what the right CSR's are.

Tim. (shoppa@triumf.ca)



