On 17 Dec 1997 17:26:58 GMT, Doug Siebert wrote:

	d> Because if they are going to change their instruction
	d> set, there is no more penalty to go to
	d> Merced rather than something of their own design.

There is a penalty.

1. Translating an existing Alpha binary to an EPIC with the Alpha ISA
   as the building block is much easier and faster than doing the same
   for an entirely new ISA viz. Merced's.

2. No x86/PA-RISC backward compatibility overhead that Merced may
   have.

The binary-to-binary translation can be made completely transparent to
the end user with a little bit of OS support.

	-Arun



