Robert Young wrote:
> 
> I have code using Vax C on VMS that uses scanf. It appears to function
> properly, waiting for a 'new line' character to be entered. Recompiled on
> Dec C on an Alpha VMS system, scanf does not appear to wait for the new line
> character. VMS is 6.1 in both cases with corresponding compatible (ie old)
> compilers..
> 
> Any ideas? I am at a loss..........
> 
> Contact vyoung@groupz.net if you have an idea.......Thanks in advance

  The problem does not necessarily have to do with the scanf
  function itself. It may relate to the changes in C RTL I/O
  subsystem as well. A small sample program demonstrating
  different behaviour with VAX C and DEC C would help (the
  smaller, the better).

  The only difference in scanf between VAX C and DEC C I'm
  aware of is processing scansets. DEC C behaviour is
  ANSI-compliant while VAX C is not.

