primarily to highlight what I perceive as a marketing bloodbath DEC
took by linking the new/future OS to a rather abrupt transition in
hardware. Sure, there were maintainance releases of Ultrix (4.4 & 4.5)
after Alpha/OSF1 intro, but folks who had just purchased
DECStation/Ultrix felt a bit sold down the river by the poor handling
of the OSF/1 for DECStation no, yes, no, debacle.  This cost DEC *lots*
