one of decay and decline, rather than renewal and revitalization.  In
order to survive, DEC *has* to change that perception for the broad
market (whatever the cause, no matter how "unfair"). Period. End of
story. Elsewise, in ten years or less, Digital will be nothing more
than a charred footnote on the ashheap of computing history.

