> : The 5500 (aka mipsfair II) has a weirdo, proprietary, undocmented
> : ``second generation' [sic] smart Ethnernet interface and (iirc) DSSI
> : via the sii asic.
> 
> Isn't the sii the SCSI controller ASIC that was used in the DECstations
> 2100/3100 ?

Yes, it's the same asic, but The chip can do both SCSI and DSSI.
(DSSI is, vaguely, like embedding the CI cluster protocol on a SCSI bus).

The PROM can boot off DSSI disks, so clearly the PROM uses the chip to
send DSSI packets, not SCSI.  Obviuosly the bulkhead connector (and
possibly other electrical setup) is for DSSI, not SCSI.

I suppose one *could* implement a DSSI driver on top of the SCSI
packet-send interface for the sii chip, if one had a DSSI spec and
sufficient time.  If it's as much work as doing a CI port driver, it
hardly seems worth the time.



