In article <3494B81B.FB734B96@halcyon.com>,
David C. Jenner <djenner@halcyon.com> wrote:
>What more recent terminals, if any, are compatible with VT105/VT120
>graphics?  By more recent, I don't necessarily mean something that is
>produced today, just what follow-on terminals were backwards compatible
>with the VT105/VT120 graphics?

I've never met a VT120, but I do recall seeing some VT105's at one point.
AFAIK, DEC dropped the VT105's method of doing graphics and went to
ReGIS with the VT125.  Later graphics terminals - the VT240, VT340,
etc. - had expanded ReGIS capabilities.

One thing that the VT125 could do was scroll text independently of the
graphics page.  Later ReGIS terminals couldn't do this.  It was
"easy" to do on the VT125 because an add-on board did all the graphcis
processing and generated the image all independently from the "main"
VT100 terminal that it was bolted on to.

Tim. (shoppa@triumf.ca)



