In article <EL7GBE.E6r@spcuna.spc.edu>, Terry Kennedy <terry@spcunb.spc.edu> writes:
:Stan Pietkiewicz <stanp@storm.ca> writes:
:> What is the  maximum memory I can install in this machine?  
:> The bottom line is; I have 3 M7622 memory boards, will this machine 
:> support more than the 2 that were originally installed? 
:
:  You're limited to 4 memory modules or the number of CD backplane slots,
:whichever comes first. As I recall (I don't work with these any more) the
:BA23 had 3 CD slots (CPU + 2 memory) and the BA123 had 4 (CPU + 3 memory).
:The BA2xx were all CD, so you could get 4 memory modules in them.

  And -- with enough CD slots, a proper five-connector ribbon cable, and
  four KA650-Bx series modules -- the system physical memory limit is 64
  megabytes.  And the M7622 is the MA650-Bx 16 megabyte memory module.

  The BA2xx enclosure is the enclosure the MicroVAX 3600 was normally sold
  with.  And the per-enclosure memory limits -- based on CD slots -- are:

        series  megabytes
	BA23	32
	BA123	48
	BA213	64 (best choice)
	BA215	64

  The BA213 has free slots left over for a reasonable configuration.  The
  BA215 has one free slot left over when used with a 64 MB configuration.

  -------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
