> What about the DS5500... a Mips machine in a Qbus BA213...


The 5500 (aka mipsfair II) has a weirdo, proprietary, undocmented
``second generation' [sic] smart Ethnernet interface and (iirc) DSSI
via the sii asic.

The 5400 (aka mipsfair) comes in a smaller Qbus, has a  Lance
ethernet interface with the same weirdo constraints as the 3100..

There's no free OS support and you're stuck with Ultrix.  (Adding 5400
support for NetBSD would be almost a cut-and-paste, but I have no
access to hardware and no incentive to do so.  The 5500 has all the
undocumented hardware).

If you want a really impressive spaceheater, don't forget the 5800
series (XMI, basically a PolarStar with mips CPU boards, iirc).

Someone else has described these machines as ``decstations in Qbus
boxes''.  Nice, but from the perspective of an OS, not entirely true.



