> It has a MIPS series chip (R3000 i think) at 20 MHz. 
> For the DS 5000/1xx, the xx denotes clock speed and the processor is an R3000.

That's correct. (r3000a, maybe.)


> The DS5000/20, /25, /33 had R4000's (R4400s? dont rmember) and the speeds
> had almost nothing to do with the numbers. 

That's not correct.  The Personal DECstations have the same CPU
daughtercard interface as the 5000/1xx.  The {20,25,33} MHz
daughtercard for the 5000/1xx and the 5000/xx are the same.

Similarly, the 50MHz r4000 daughtercard for the 5000/150 and 5000/50
are the same.  Reliable sources say the only difference in the upgrade
kits is the front bezel.


> The 5000/200 has an R3000 at 25 MHz and the '240 and '260 have quite fast
> R3400 and R4400 respectively- i think. 
40Mhz r3400 and 60Mhz r4400.  

This information is all on the NetBSD/pmax web page, amongst other
places. The NetBSD web page should also have a list of other info PROM
revisions and known bugs.

>please correct me if im making mistakes here!

You're welcome :).



