V. Scalo wrote:
> 
> My company is using vax
> 
> and is proably going to go with an ibm aix system
> 
> is there anyway to tie the new system into the old for
> applications that we won't be able to transfer over?
> 


There are several options that I know of. Some less desireable than
others.

1. Use a Bit3 PCI to Qbus converter and an ABLE Qniverter - UGLY but
I've seen it done in the past.  Of course this requires new software for
the OLD Unibus specialized interfaces.

2. I believe that The LOGICAL Co. has a DR11 interface on a PCI, this is
a general purpose DMA interface that can be used for high speed computer
to computer communication and there are drivers in the decus library for
the Qbus and Unibus versions.  Of course this too would require software
on the AIX side, but might be easier to do.

3. We've had SUN and IBM applications using Bit3 and Qniverters.

4. We've had a few request for a PCI to Unibus converter that could be
used for the various PC and Alpha emulations.  If there was enough
interest, I think ABLE could be convinced to do one.



