Tim Shoppa <shoppa@alph02.triumf.ca> wrote:
>But - and this is the thing I never understood about Bitcom -
>*REAL VT100'S HANDLE VT52 SEQUENCES*.  I swear, it seems like 90%
>of the people who make and sell emulators have never read a VT100
>user's manual, nor have they ever tested their product against
>a real VT100 to find all the ways in which their emulator falls flat
>on its face.

I've run into the opposite problem a few times -- people who think that
the VT100's emulation of the VT52 is any good!  The VT52 support in RPI's
terminal concentrators assigns one of the commonly used keys to PF4, which
of course a real VT52 doesn't have, but RPI didn't know that because
they only tested on a VT100 in "VT52" mode.  Also, the VT100's graphics
character set is all different, it sends a different WRU string, it has no
"hold screen" mode (well OK that was an annoying feature anyway, I cut the
traces to my "hold screen" key and wired it to the UART MSB so I'd have a
real Meta key for TOPS-20 EMACS) and its tabs could be anywhere unlike the
VT52 where they're always every 8 columns (and on the slightly strange VT62
they're every 8 columns until you get near the right margin, then they
shrink).

John Wilson
