We have a Cabriolet with 32MB under Linux, running X, and I have never
noticed the small amount of memory as a bottleneck; granted, we don't
do much with it, currently it runs just a few daemons and an rc5
challenge, and it's usually used only by a single simultaneous user,
but I would not recommend buying a UDB for heavier use. Anyway, here's
the current output of free:

             total       used       free     shared    buffers     cached
Mem:         29464      27760       1704      17024       6800       9960
