Swap:       523640       2240     521400

> 96 MB would be better and 128 MB quite ok.

We are using a 128MB Cabriolet for 5-10 simultaneous users, who do
serious work and (what's worse) use Netscape on this machine; we have
no serious memory problem (but the first keypress on an emacs that was
not used for an hour often takes a few seconds to process). This is
under Digital Unix, but I doubt that DU is more frugal in it's memory
use than Linux.

