bundled with many new modems.  It has two kinds of VT100 emulation, vt100a
and vt100b (its terminology); the latter also handles VT52 sequences.  It
is fully customizable via emulator script files (in fact all functions can
be customizable via script files).  It comes with a companion BitFax
package which does what the name implies, along with phone book, etc.
functions.  The programs seem to be written in assembly language and they
are fast and responsive.

Their address is Bit Software, Inc., 47987 Fremont Blvd., Fremont CA
94538; (510) 490-9470 voice, -2939 fax.  I don't have the URL but I'm sure
an Altavista or similar search could find it (I'm not associated with them
at all; usual disclaimers, etc. etc.  I just have had good results with
them and am passing on the info). 

