If I remember right, a BREAK isn't really a character in the ASCII sense,
but a SPACE condition on the line for more that a mumbledy milliseconds.
That's why a power glitch, or power cycling the console, forces a reboot
(SPACE = 0 VDC logic = +12 VDC RS-232) - jc

Richard Tomkins (neuron@cyberus.ca) wrote:
: I agree, it could well be a break character. I had a similar problem, the
: machine would reboot at weird times. Turned out the terminal was going
: south, would crowbar it's power supply and when It came back on, it
: triggered a reboot on the machine.
