In article <34889E03.3C38@storm.ca>, Stan Pietkiewicz <stanp@storm.ca> wrote:
> What is the 20 pin header connector on the front end (opposite the 50-pin 
> and power) on this drive for??
> 
> I picked up a couple of these, and I'd like to know a bit more about them 
> before I power them up.....

I'm going out on a limb and assume, since this was posted at the same time as a
query on a SCSI board, that you think they're SCSI disks and plan to hook the
two together.  They're not SCSI. They're DSSI disks.  DSSI is what resulted
when some mad DEC engineers in some dark dungeon of DEC's old mill building
crossed SCSI with CI. :-)

You want either the DEC QBUS-DSSI adaptor board (KFQSA?) or find someone who
wants DSSI disks in exchange for SCSI disks.

-Mike



