X-Deja-AN: 296475373
Organization: neuron, technology consultants
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


I have had a number of reports and today looked into the issue with two systems.

Applying the Microsoft Service Pack 3 to a Alpha running Windows NT V4.0
will result in an unstable system. Microsoft unfortunately replaces the
HAL code with an older version.

On a AlphaServer 1000A and an AlphaServer 4100 I installed Windows NT. I
then copied the OS subtree into the temp directory for safekeeping. After
that, I applied Microsoft Service Pack 3 for Windows NT. In both cases,
the HAL in the OS subtree was replaced with an older and not up to rev.
version. I copied the OS subtree back from the temp directory to itself
and all was fine.

I caution users of Alpha based systems, if you are experiencing random
crashes and unstable operations, take a close look at the HAL code. For
some, this will actually mean taking a look at the Hardware Support Floppy
Disk that came with your system, as it has a more recent HAL than that on
the Windows NT V4.0 CD-ROM itself.

If anyone would like to complain, please feel free to e-mail Bill Gates
and encourage his firm to improve the quality of his product set.

rtt

