In large companies sometimes you don't know how or who makes decisions.  I
would agree that DEC seems to have a bad rap, often for no reason that I can
see.

I work as an engineer, we use Unix workstations.  The loyalty seems to be:

1. Sys Admins like Suns
2. engineers, smarting from several years of old, slow Suns (the new Ultras are
decent) like HP's.  
3. There are a few SGI advocates around

Two years ago we go 4 brands of boxes in fordemo:  sgi, sun, hp, and DEC.   DEC
beat all in speed 2 to 1.   We bought Sun and hp. Why?

The main reason was that one software maker (Cadence) pulled out of the DEC
platform.   Software availability rules.  We need boxes that can run any needed
package.  This favors the most widely sold box.

Andrew



