, Varga Akos Endre <hamster@pc0176sd.sysdata.siemens.at> writes:
|>I have a question about the VAX10000...
|>
|>When was it introduced? What was it? :) I know nothing about it,
|>never seen one, and the first place I saw it mentioned was on
|>the Digital website... Could someone help me? 

The VAX 10000 and its smaller sibling, the VAX 7000 (platform codenames
LAZER/BLAZER) were introduced in July 1992.  They were "mainframe class"
systems that could accomodate up to four processors.  They could be upgraded
by board-swap to "DEC 10000 AXP" and "DEC 7000 AXP" Alpha-based systems.
Pricing started at about $760,000.  The processor was a 91MHz NVAX with
a "VUPS" rating of about 35.  This platform later evolved into "Turbolaser",
today's AlphaServer 8000 family.
