Stan Pietkiewicz wrote:

> Yes, I realize they're DSSI, not SCSI, and that's why I'm asking...
>
> Will these disks run without a front panel? Is the disk ID dependent on its
> positions in the chassis, or is it set by the front panel? (If it's set via
> the FP, that takes care of Q1;-}) )

It depends on the machine wheter RF disks will run without a front panel. If
you're
using a VAX4000-200/MicroVAX 3300  in a BA215 (floor standing), there is no
need for a front panel, because some kind of frontpanel with ID Plugs is alread
build
in the BA215. Then you will need a E-SF version of the Drive

If you're using a VAX4000-300 in a BA 400 (also floor standing, but bigger),
you will
need E-AF mounting kits WITH a front panel.

If you'r using a SF 200, than the SF will take care of the IDs, but I'll assume
you do not
have a VAX6000 ;-)

The ID is NOT depending on the position of the chassis, it's only depending on
the ID Plug,
so make sure the ID Plugs are unique. The UNIT NUMBER is determined by the Plug

OR by software (when using FORCEUNIT).

Chris





