I've heard of a few folks intercepting system services for a process to lie to it
about the date/time. For a basic system service intercept, check out SSINT
by Brian Schenkenberger; see the V3 freeware CD or recent sigtapes
for a copy. It's source code and you'll need to poke it to do what you want
for $gettim and friends (and you really should arrange that the faked time change
with time also), but it is also perfectly reasonable to just use a workstation and
set its time to a future date. For amusement make it AFTER 2038. VMS will have
no grief here, but after that date, the unix seconds-since-1/1/1970 becomes negative
to 32 bits. Just challenge your friends running unix to run correctly as of 1/1/2039.
I've heard that Microsoft stuff fails well before that, but have not tried it personally.


