In article <66999f$js8$1@rockcake.bt.net>, McCormackJ@RocketMail.Com (Jonathan McCormack) writes:
>Hi,
>
>I upgraded my AS to 7.1 from 6.2-1H1 and UCX & DECNET don't work anymore.  They 
>start up OK, but I can't ping anyone and vice-versa, and I can't set host to 
>anybody.  It's like the network card isn't recognised anymore.  If I restore 
>6.2-1H1 everything is fine.
>
>Can anybody give me some help on this?

Are you sure, that UCX & DECnet starts ok ?

I'm pretty sure, you need to reinstall UCX V4.1 (or apply an ECO after the
upgrade) and install DECnet V7.1 or DECnet-Plus V7.1 after the OpenVMS V7.1
upgrade.

If you installed DECnet-Plus with OpenVMS V7.1 and didn't configure it,
then a mis-behaviour is expected ;-)

If you installed DECnet-Plus with OpenVMS V7.1, deinstalled it then to install
DECnet Ph4 again, it might be possible, that the Ph4 config files were deleted.

It might also be possible, that you use old net hardware, which is not
supported by the V7.1 software (though I currently don't know a card, which
is supported with V6.2 but not with V7.1). It did happen before, with eg. DEQNA

It might also be possible, that you use very new net hardware, which is not
yet supported by the V7.1 software but is supported with the hardware release
V6.2-1H2 or V7.1-1H1 (But AFAIK V7.1 includes all hardware support of all the
V6.2-1Hx hardware releases). AFAIK V7.1-1H1 is required for the DE500-BB

Have you entered the invocation of SYS$STARTUP:SYS$NET_SERVICES.COM in your
SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM ? See the SYS$STARTUP:SYSTARTUP_VMS.TEMPLATE for more info.

What does SHOW NETWORK/FULL show ?

just my 0.02
