In article <66kp5t$9e5@bgtnsc01.worldnet.att.net>, Kevin Landry 
<klandry@worldnet.att.net> writes:
|>I am running an Alpha OpenVMS 7.1.  I am trying to capture an ASCII file
|>from our Alpha onto a PC using an old version of Procomm, the file
|>contains one record (comma delimited).  The file that I end up with on
|>the PC side is strange however.  The 1st line is 950 characters in
|>length with a carriage return/linefeed at 950.  The subsequent lines are
|>81 characters in length.  Is there some setting that I need to adjust on
|>the Alpha?  Procomm's settings are correct as I have used the same
|>script and settings in Procomm with another platform (MAI Basic-4) and I
|>have never had a problem with CR/LF's showing up in the middle of
|>records.

How are you doing the "capture"?  Are you using a transfer program such
as KERMIT or ZMODEM, or are you TYPEing the file on VMS and relying on
Procomm's session capture?  If the latter, then the VMS terminal driver is
likely to insert CRLFs when it thinks it ought to.

I'd suggest using a transfer program - I use ZMODEM with Procomm (the latest
"32" version) and it works fine.  KERMIT would also work well.
