In article <348DA285.5F63@advicom.net>, "Ronnie M. Lajoie" <hal5@advicom.net> writes:
>
>I recently purchased a DECstation 3100 at a surplus sale.
>It came with only a VT420 dumb terminal (monitor and keyboard).

Did it come with a loopback connector on the mouse plug?  When
use as a non-workstation you must have the mouse loopback.  I
don't know the pin-outs for the mouse loopback, but they may
be in the ULTRIX FAQ which can be found somewhere under:

ftp://www.digitial.com/pub/DEC

>The machine powers up but nothing appears on the VT420 display.

If you have the mouse loopback, make sure the VT420 is on the
right tty port.  You want the one with the printer icon.  I
think the default baud rate is 9600, you might try putting the
terminal through all the choices.

>I came across only one message implying that the DS3100 must
>have a DEC monitor and DEC keyboard plugged in to work, and
>the writer made it sound like it was not the dumb terminal.

The DECstation 3100 can be configured as a workstation using
the approiate mouse, keyboard and monitor depending on the
graphics option installed (monochrome frame buffer or 8 plane
color frame buffer), or a DECsystem 3100 without the frame
buffer and with a terminal and mouse loopback.  You might
also want to check to see if there is frame buffer installed,
since that would make the console firmware that that it was
a DECstation.

>What do I need to do to get this machine to boot, or at least
>send some hardware test information to the screen?  Even with
>the VT420 plugged in, all the DS3100 rear indicator lights
>are red "7654 3210".

Below is a transcription of the self-test section of the DECstation
3100 maintenance guide.  Beyond that it says at the bottom for all
the light being on, I don't know what that particular combination
means:


    Self Test Failures

	When a DECstation 3100 is powered on it performs a number
	of self tests.  The normal completion of these tests looks
	something like:

		KN01 V6.71

		7..6..5..4..3..2..1..0

		16Mb..........0

		KN01 V6.71
		08-00-2b-0d-f7-6a
		0x01000000
		>>

	If a test fails, the last number displayed is that of the
	test that failed.  The message "FAILURE - RESET TO CONTINUE"
	may also be displayed.  The individual self test failures
	are:

	Test Code	Component		Action to take
	------------------------------------------------------------
