> numbers for each type of chip (say PII 300 vs Alpha 533)?

In order of performance:

                                               SPECint95  SPECfp95

 21164a  600MHz   (LX mobo with 2MB cache)      18.4       21.3

 21164a  500MHz   (LX mobo with 2MB cache)      15.7       19.5

 21164PC 533MHz   (SX mobo with 1MBcache)       12.4       16.1

 PII     300MHz   (Intel 440LX mobo)            11.7        8.15

So in SPECint95, the 600MHz Alpha is to a PII 300 what a PII 300 is to
a 180MHz PPro.

And in SPECfp95, the Alpha beats the PII 300 the way a PII 300
wacks a Pentium 133.

That said, a 600 MHz Alpha system will set you back maybe
$5K to $6K.

21164a 533MHz systems  can be had for under $3K  (sans monitor)

21164PC 533MHz systems can be had for under $2K (sans monitor)

Don't know what PII/300 systems with the 440LX mobo go for.

The PII and 21164a numbers above are from http://www.specbench.org/
The 21164pc numbers were provided by Burkhard Neidecker-Lutz, a source
who's proven in the past to be very reliable. The 21164pc numbers were
measured running NT(!).

