On second thought and as a good general rule of thumb for everyone, if you
update the firmware re-run the ECU pertinent to the Operating System you
are running. This will avoid complications and funny problems later on.
This should be done even if you do not have any EISA options currently
installed in the machine in question.

On another note, those applying Microsoft Service Releases should know
that the Microsoft people messed up, they overwrite your HAL code with
that of an earlier release. This usually manifests itself as the system
becoming unstable shortly after applying Service Pack 3 to Windows NT.
You'll have to go back and get the updated HAL for you machine from the
floppy disk that DIGITAL supplied as applicable to your hardware platform.

