In a previous note (below), I mentioned my difficulties getting a Hayes Accura 
56K modem to function in a Starion 600i.  I have finally gotten it operational.

I ended up installing the Hayes modem to Com2 IRQ3 (normal settings) and 
jumpered the modem portion of the Boca SE1440 to com3 IRQ4 (intentionally 
creating an IRQ conflict with Com 1).  The plug n play utility indicated it was 
setting the Boca modem to IRQ 11, but failed to override hardware jumpering.  
Apparently the Boca SE1440 is only half plug-n-play; it handles the sound 
portion without difficulty, but the modem relies on the jumpers.  As for the 
conflicting IRQ 4 (com1 and com3), there isn't an operational conflict since I 
only use com 1 for a serial label printer that's never used during a 
communication session.

As for the Sound Blaster card.... I'll unload it.  I only picked it up because 
the support guy at Boca said I couldn't have two modems in the PC unless I was 
running Win95.  Taking what he said at face value, I decided to get rid of the 
Boca card altogether and needed a stand-alone sound card to replace it.  
Perhaps he should have said I could only use one of two modems installed in one 
machine.  

