To: Edward Lee <edlee@chinet.chinet.com>
Organization: System Management Associates
Reply-To: LEVY.M@ACM.ORG
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


Edward Lee wrote:
> 
> Is it at all possible to make a PC164SX motherboard with the 21164PC
> processor accept non-ECC SDRAM DIMMs?  Would it be a matter of an AlphaBIOS
> upgrade?  The non-ECC SDRAMs seem to be more readily available and to be
> selling at lower prices.
> 
> -Ed L

No, ECC is required.  There's no AlphaBIOS version that I'm aware of
that changes that.

Non-ECC SDRAMS are cheaper for a reason: they don't have the chips to
implement ECC.  Fewer chips, lower cost.  You really want the ECC, it
will keep your machine from crashing on single bit errors.  ECC stands
for "Error Correcting Code" and it's good stuff.

--

