I have RT-11 V5.01c.  The monitor's code affecting Y2K is only in two
places and is easily replaced by editing the source and re-SYSGENning.  If
you don't use date rollover, then you only need to add a bit of code to
KMOVLY.MAC.  One might even be able to insert it with SIPP but it's easier
to edit the source (see http://tribeca.ios.com/~nickz/dec.html).  The
other utilities like DIR are much more difficult to fix.  In V5.01 they
print "-10x" for the year 200x (<2004) and "-BAD-" for 2004 and up.  The
Macro-11 assembler also has a similar problem, and the day of the week it
prints would be off too.  A stopgap measure might be to use the code
written to update the monitor and make a standalone program out of it to
read and set file dates and the system date.  Or one could get V5.7.

