In article <34837515.4EA6@storm.ca>, Stan Pietkiewicz <stanp@storm.ca> writes:
> I have a feeling this may be a FAQ, but I haven't seen the answer
> anywhere, so here goes:
>   Can a DEC (Alpha) 3000 model 400s run without a graphics console? aka
> headless, with just a vt-type terminal for a console?

        Absolutely, we've been doing so for  a number of years.  The "s"
    in  "400s" means "server" so I expect many (most?) of the 3000/400s'
    were bought headless (but perhaps not).

        You need to find the "Alternate console switch", which is marked
    "S3", on the back of the server and put it in the down position (I'm
    looking in the "Owner's Guide" for the AXP 3000/400s, pages 2-12 and
    2-13).  Then plug your VT terminal into  the MMJ port just above and
    to the _right_ of the switch (the one directly above has a telephone
    icon  and is for a modem; the one you want has a  printer/left-right
    arrow icon).   At  this  point,  you  need  neither  a  monitor  nor
    keyboard: the VT terminal is your console.

> Any thing to watch out for in an arrangement like this??

        Not that I know of...

            -Ken
