VAXServer was in fact a MicroVAX 3100, either model 10 or model 20,
pre-loaded with OpenVMS VAX and PATHWORKS.
You have a MV3100. The model 10 was was a low profile unit, and may have
had a floppy disk drive, tape drive or CD-ROM in it's front panel, or
nothing at all. The model 20 was a taller chassis and had a pop open front
door, behind which, 2 5.25" peripherals could have been placed.

All the model 10 units and most VAXstations had the same power supply. The
model 20 units had a differnet power supply, more current capacity.

The power supply LED blinking is indicative of the crowbar in operation,
thus you have a short somewhere. Pull out that disk drive you just added
and look at the power connector, it's probably wired wrong, like +12 and
+5 mixed or maybe even the grounds mixed with +5 or +12.

